## Context
Decorrelation today is prose: no code resolves a reviewer's family and no
test checks "different family from producer". The only enforced lever is the
tier pin, which this redesign removes (and which may already be inert, see
1063). Every Claude Code subagent is Anthropic, so cross-family review means a
headless CLI seat via the launch doors of 1064; the mechanism exists in
`skills/review-pr/SKILL.md:151-186` (detached-seat substitution, `no report`,
never simulate).

Contradictions to fix: `rules/workflow.md:107` says other-vendor reviewers
"stronger" while skills pin reviewers below the coder; "sibling minimum" is
defined nowhere; `rules/claude-code.md:41-42` claims the rightsizing test
enforces reviewer-below-coder (it does not); `profiles/coder/PROFILE.md:29-30`
claims reviewers are decorrelated "by construction".

## Scope
- Rule: an independent review seat comes from a different FAMILY than the
  producer, checked against the grid `family` field; when none is reachable,
  say so in the report. Name the three axes (angle, lineage, replication) and
  when replication may substitute (folds in 1057).
- Default on a Claude-produced PR: attempt one cross-family detached seat
  through the cheapest live door in `routes.json`; else `no report` and
  `PANEL-INTEGRITY: DEGRADED`. Cost is real (OpenRouter 60 USD/month cap,
  OpenAI credit wall); state it.
- Attribution: derive family from the provider prefix of `model`; use the
  existing `model-state=runtime-masked` for Vibe. Add a field only for lineage
  twins the grid labels.
- Mechanical floor: a test that every launch line in a skill body names an
  explicit model choice, so an omitted choice fails CI instead of silently
  inheriting the session model.
- Fix the contradictions above; may ship with "no cross-family seat reachable,
  say so" as the only behaviour if the doors of 1064 slip.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Doctrine written in the review skills' shared reference or rules, with the three axes
- [ ] The contradictions listed above are fixed
- [ ] The mechanical-floor test exists and fails on a launch line with no model choice
- [ ] A gaze run on a Claude-produced PR gets a non-Claude seat or reports `no report` with `DEGRADED`
- [ ] `make check` passes
